														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4864526">
									

<p>Omega-7 was a much earlier version of the team that was disbanded after SCP-076 (who was a member) went berserk and an entire Site was nuked to stop him. I know you said you didn't want to read details, but the story is <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-076-2">here.</a> It's a lot shorter than the Alpha-9 stuff.</p>
<p>Alpha-9 comes from the Resurrection canon, where the idea of an anomalous humanoid SCP MTF was, well, resurrected. <a href="/scp-105">SCP-105</a> is the only member of Omega-7 who is also in Alpha-9. I don't know the current state of the Resurrection canon, but I'm pretty sure they aren't actually fully approved and in action in that canon.</p>
<hr />
<p>A word to the wise: Outside of the fiction, most SCPs that were in Omega-7 or were written to be in Omega-7 were deleted due to low quality. If you're thinking about writing a humanoid SCP into an MTF, be careful, you're heading into rough waters.</p>
<p>Honestly, most of the anomalous humanoids I know of in MTFs have their own specific MTFs instead of being in Alpha-9, and even then you still need to justify it. For example, Tau-5 sees a lot of use beyond their original stories, whereas I'm pretty sure Alpha-9 is only talked about in that particular canon.</p>

