<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> SCP-XXXX Is a spiral stairwell underneath a lighthouse located outside of Koror, Palau. The stairwell contains writings written with plantlife in an unknown language. Anybody can read it, but no cognitohazards have been identified.<br />
Near the bottom of the stairwell is an entity observed to write the text on the walls. It has an appearance similar to a wendigo glowing a bright white color. people to entity as &quot;the Null walker&quot; when never given its name. It's docile but can cause illusions to provokers.<br />
At the bottom of the stairwell is a bioluminescent cave with more text and unidentified life.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> In the first exploration, a D-Class was to record the texts and descend as low as he can. He was able to find the Null walker, but what happened next was unknown.<br />
In the second exploration log, a 3 man MTF team was to continue exploration with better equipment. 5 hours in, the leader of the MTF goes into the stairwell alone and tells nobody to follow him. After 30 minutes, he is found to have committed suicide by gunshot, with a note saying that the Null walker will reincarnate him and keep him from harm. The next day he was found continuing his daily routine, with no recollection of the event.<br />
A 4 person MTF team was to have a more permanent exploration in the final exploration log. A Cognito hazard specialist, Linguistic, Anomalous biologist, and a psychologist were sent. The cognitohazard specialist and the linguist went missing, and later the linguist was found dead and killed by the Cognitohazard specialist (who is missing). The biologist and the psychologist team up and cut off the connection to control. One month later, they are also found in their daily routine with no recollection of the event.<br />
In the end, they find journals belonging to the biologist and previous MTFs. In the biologist's journal, she talks about how she and the psychologist looked out for each other and how they killed the cognitohazard specialist. After they went down to the bottom of the stairwell and found the giant bioluminescent cave and the D-classes' animated bodies and the previous MTF, were glowing blue and showed no intelligence.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> This SCP gives an urge for both the foundation and the readers to find out what is at the bottom of the stairwell.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> None</p>

