														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4864507">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> An indestructible and immortal crusader is on a quest to rid the world of SCP's either by killing them or cleansing them of their &quot;corruption.&quot;</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> An MTF Squad is out looking for an SCP that had escaped containment, but instead end up finding the Crusader after having just killed it. They take him into custody, and quickly realize just what they have found and make a deal with him. Discovering unlike other SCP's, once you take away his &quot;blessed&quot; weapons and shield he's just your everyday, immortal, above average human male wearing crusader armor, the Foundation makes him an offer. He begrudgingly agrees and helps the Foundation to capture or kill dangerous SCP’s. Twice, when sent on a mission to capture a new SCP, the Crusader disobeys orders, killing one SCP but helping another escape before letting either one be identified. The second time becomes the last straw, and when questioned, it becomes apparent that up to this point all that mattered was his quest, but this is a much more personal matter that he refuses to share with the Foundation. The only things he ends up telling the Foundation is that many others also believed the knowledge they would gain would outweigh the danger, and that not all birds were meant to be caged.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> The Foundation is always seeking anti anomalous SCP's to help contain other SCP's or put down dangerous ones. But are they willing to compromise and negotiate to achieve that goal? Would they set aside their own beliefs, ideals, and processes for ultimately the greater good, or choose to lose such an asset for the sake of doing things their way? At what point, will they refuse to compromise any further?</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> While I’m a fast learner, I don’t have the time or the will to go through every SCP Article, Tale, and Group of Interest. If something here has already been done, or is too similar to something else please let me know.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

